fjarr (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Desktop (new, fjarr.desktop): the robot's screen in the browser, on GNOME
    (Wayland) and on an X11 kiosk. Every monitor is a track that follows
    hot-plug, a session can add virtual monitors, the operator drives it with
    keyboard and pointer (a drag crosses monitors), the clipboard works both
    ways (text and PNG images) and the robot's cursor is shown. GNOME capture
    is DMA-BUF into the encoder without a copy (ADR-0041).
  * Desktop packages: fjarr-desktop-session (the session helper, which hands
    the agent only its capture's PipeWire node), fjarr-desktop-wayland and
    fjarr-desktop-x11; setup desktop and --undo desktop, ghost screens for a
    headless robot, and a desktop with the agent in a container.
  * Audio (new, fjarr.audio): the robot's microphones as Opus tracks for a
    session granted listen; talking through its speaker with talk
    (push-to-talk); the desktop's own sound on GNOME and X11.
  * Agent: a signaling socket whose pings go unanswered is dropped within
    45 s and the agent reconnects; it used to look online for ~15 min after
    its uplink died (docs/08#transport-layers).
  * Agent: a Fjarr tunnel interface never carries ICE (#34).
  * Media: stopping the thumbnail tier could freeze every tier (#38); a bad
    viewer drags a shared encoder down for 2 s, not ~7 (#40); a returning
    track keeps its SSRC's sequence numbers; the sharpness preference.
  * Terminal: a shell that refuses logins is reported, not started.
  * Packaging: /run/fjarr exists after install, and --check without root
    says why it cannot look.
  * Server: a WebSocket ping on every socket every 30 s, and a socket that
    answers none for two intervals is ended and its peer told.
  * fjarr-connect: wss:// signaling (it failed against any hosted server);
    prints what a person needs and no library logs by default.

 -- Fjarr <dev@fjarr.io>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:01:31 +0100

fjarr (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Agent: stopping a quality tier moments after starting it no longer leaks
    or hangs the agent (the tier's elements are locked before teardown).
  * Agent: a track's media flows only once the viewer's answer accepted it;
    a track the answer rejected is refused. Removing such a track could hang
    the agent's core loop (docs/08#track-control).
  * Agent: a request sent as soon as the control channel opens is no longer
    lost when the agent is busy; fjarr-connect's unanswered open (#33).
  * Agent: reads /etc/fjarr/fjarr.toml when no --config is given.
  * Containers: the reference compose file (apt.fjarr.io/docker-compose.yml);
    the image creates the tunnel device and drops to fjarr with no
    capabilities; setup, net setup and --check work without systemd.

 -- Fjarr <dev@fjarr.io>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 07:47:20 +0200

fjarr (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The first published release. 0.1.0 reached testing only: its arm64
    image needed intel-media-va-driver, which has no arm64 build.

